  "id": "visually-guided-reaching",
  "term": "visually guided reaching",
  "definition": "Visually guided reaching is reaching toward a target while using visual information about the target and one’s hand position, such as a cursor representing the hand on a screen. It is a goal-directed action that depends on coordination among sensory, cognitive, and motor systems.",
